                <pb facs="0384" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg302"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 815.00/1157.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Commissioner to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Puerto Cortes</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-04"><hi rendition="#italic">March 4,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Dawson reports the receipt of a telegram of this date from Dávila accepting
                    the peace arrangement; that the President and Vice President are expected to
                    resign and that Congress will elect Bertrand as first designate.</p>
            </div>
